/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/nexus-topology.mem:15:role       = "the DEPLOYMENT topology under the two-axis mesh, and the CIVIC-SCALE TLS ledger (researched 2026-08-08): which public name serves which Nexus, at which layer, for whose glass. The first Nexus at *.amorphousdreams.net and the second at *.elyncia.net; elyncia.app RESERVED for the mobile surface, where the TLD's own HSTS preload makes every name under it a SECURE CONTEXT BY CONSTRUCTION — a load-bearing property against the crypto.subtle wall, never a branding choice. Three serving layers (household LAN via split-horizon · a contracted operator's own LAN under delegated challenge labels · the cloud shelf for the general internet), and the law that holds them together: a Nexus name grants RENDEZVOUS, never IDENTITY, so every layer stays severable. RENEWAL INVERTS: a central renewal queue IS a roster, so each operator holds their own key and account and the blessing rides a DNS record, never a certificate — EAB does NOT carry this (CA-to-customer only); the BR Parent/Subordinate ACME Account exception names it but no CA implements it; dns-persist-01 sits staging-only; GTS dns-account-01 stands LIVE. Rate limits cap ONBOARDING RATE, not fleet size (ARI renewals exempt, overrides inherit). A child CAA record REPLACES its parent whole, so a shared wildcard and per-operator pinning cannot coexist. The offline-serving window shrinks 60d to 43d (2027-02-10) to 30d (2028-02-16). NO expiry safety net exists — the mesh carries its own witness, alarmed at ~80% elapsed. Two gates already live: multi-perspective validation (the public authoritative view answers the whole internet unfiltered) and mandatory DNSSEC at the delegation boundary."
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/nexus-topology.mem:70:''THE OPERATOR'S LIFT, bounded.'' A contracted operator stands ''one resolver'' and routes their own LAN. They MUST NOT hold apex write on a Nexus zone. What they hold instead: a delegated `_acme-challenge` label for their own subtree, which splits ''proof of control'' from ''zone custody'' — the operator proves control of what they serve, and the Nexus never handles their key material (#attestation-plane, the cadence law).
