oured in 9 of 65 themes while every gate read green).\n21\tD4 — SIX independent readings of the `/^OWED/` prefix at five instrument sites; three strip the\n22\t`READER <version>` prefix first, and `bracket-witness.js` and `light-cone.js` DO NOT — so the day a\n23\t`READER <v> OWED` row lands in swallow-ledger or bracket-ledger, swallow reads it owed and light-cone\n24\treads it ruled, and light-cone's own gate goes quiet on it. 76 live `READER … OWED` rows today, all\n25\tin darkness-ledger.\n26\tD5 — judgements live in TWO homes: 20 corpus/*.txt and 9 JSON data tiddlers; colour-witness reads\n27\tone of each.\n28\tD6 — three tools wearing a flag account for six gates (engine/behaviour, still/reach,\n29\toverreach-host/cut). D7 — snap-tid and snap-meta are one tool, one scope, two globs.\n30\tD8 — a duplication the house's own ward CANNOT SEE: one-implementation.test.js filters out\n31\t`*.test.js`, and inside that blind spot sit a byte-identical `scopesOn` helper in two invariants and\n32\t`source ./grammars.sh` inlined in two more — the exact work tokenizer.js holds.\n33\t\n34\t## Vocabulary drifts\n35\tV1 file-kind suffix: 12 ledger-shaped files, only 10 named `-ledger`; expected-divergence and\n36\tmust-fail are unsuffixed ledgers; 7 single-number ratchets split 4 floor / 3 ceiling, and\n37\t`attribute-kind-ceiling` holds a count that may FALL while `coverage-floor` holds one that may RISE —\n38\tthe filename encodes direction and gets it wrong once. colour-pair exists as both a ledger and a floor.\n39\tV2 three spellings of over-reading (OVERREACH / overbound / overreach).\n40\tV3 `MISS` is a HOMONYM across two ledgers that share one codec (line-grain dark vs character-grain\n41\tunmarked).\n42\tV4 four words for one lifecycle: stale / explains nothing / retires against `unruled` which names the\n43\topposite side; `idle` already exists in divergence-staleness and has not won.\n44\tV5 eight reason prefixes; only HOST and READER have a shared reader.\n45\tV6 444