s-ledgers.test.js\n69\t\"Thirteen\" (20), GateReport-Doc \"Seventeen\" (49/65), theme-model.test.js \"Four gates\" (12 requirers),\n70\ttokenizer.test.js \"Twenty-two instruments\" (26).\n71\t\n72\t## Dead and aliased\n73\tDead: `echo-test`, `list-test`, `run_snapshots.sh` (19 lines at the root, referenced by nothing but\n74\titself; snapshot-check.js does the work; no ward can see it). Aliased/narrowing: tests-advanced,\n75\ttests-basic, tests-htmltiddler, tests-wikitext. Refuted collapse candidates kept: still-breadth.js and\n76\ttw5-oracle-path.js look unreferenced but run as child processes inside swapped-grammar sandboxes.\n77\tCI: the `compose` job duplicates what the `gates` job already runs — an exact duplicate job.\n78\t\n79\t## Where YIN suspects a collapse would LOSE something and cannot prove it — YOUR seam\n80\tA. 50 of 87 fixtures assert no scope vocabulary a snapshot does not already carry — but the measure is\n81\t   VOCABULARY, not scope-at-position, and a fixture pins intent with the law written beside it. YIN\n82\t   says which of the 50 carry a law is YANG's to rule.\n83\tB. The colour cluster: nine gates, each header distinguishing itself from its neighbours with a\n84\t   number YIN did not re-run.\n85\tC. overreach ×4: whether tests/samples/*.tw surfaces any class corpus/**/*.tw does not — unmeasured,\n86\t   and LEDGER:1352 warns the shape exists in the other direction.\n87\tD. The three flag-pairs and the two-glob pair: trivially cheap to fuse, but the harvest keys on each\n88\t   gate's own summary line and the report reads \"49 of 49\".\n89\tE. carrier-ledger vs swallow-ledger: identical row grammar; carrier-ledger refuses the fusion in its\n90\t   own words; YIN could not confirm all 7 carrier rows lack a corpus specimen.\n91\tF. prose-reading-ledger vs PlainConstructs: two homes, one shape; the stated distinction is real in\n92\t   the instruments but YIN did not verify the two populations are disjoint.\n93\tG. unasked-regions-ceiling vs swallow-ledger: coverage against correctness; the 97-region population\n94\t   unconfirmed.\n95\tH. The debt backlogs: ablation-ledger 330 of 359 rows OWED, darkness-ledger 93 of 111. Whether these\n96\t   are enumerated backlogs or guards that stopped guarding decides the fate of the two largest corpus\n97\t   files. YIN did not read the 423 reasons.\n98\tI. syntaxes/attic SHIPS: .vscodeignore names no syntaxes/attic and package-contents checks manifest →\n99\t   package only, never package → needed, so a 14KB dead sketch grammar rides into every install.\n100\t   Inferred from source, NOT confirmed by building a .vsix.\n101\tJ. 63 `punctuation.separator` sites unread; either a fifth unstated naming law exists or it is accretion.\n102\t\n103\t## YIN's ranked collapse list (17 items, in order)\n104\t1 delete run_snapshots.sh + echo-test + list-test · 2 retire four narrowing test aliases ·\n105\t3 one `owedOf()` beside `readerOf()` · 4 the byte-identical helper and the inlined grammars.sh, AND\n106\tlift one-implementation's `.test.js` exclusion · 5 snap-tid + snap-meta · 6 drop the duplicate CI\n107\tcompose job · 7 one home for the migration headline (fixes two wrong 111s) · 8 derive 65 and BAR ·\n108\t9 generate the README gate list's completeness check, keep the curated prose · 10 fix the four stale\n109\tpresent-tense counts · 11 swallow-witness ⊂ still --over --reach (HIGHEST RISK; do not attempt\n110\twithout re-running both) · 12 three sentinels into one module · 13 corpus file naming to\n111\t-ledger/-ratchet with direction in the first comment · 14 MISS → dark/unmarked · 15 one lifecycle\n112\tvocabulary (idle/unruled/retired) · 16 move gate-report's archaeology paragraph into the LEDGER ·\n113\t17 keep syntaxes/attic out of the .vsix (verify by building one first).\n114\t"}]},"uuid":"18615286-b2fc-4aed-9bd3-6ec49fd5d688","timestamp":"2026-10-07T16:32:20.088Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/joshu/.claude/jobs/86a17260/tmp/trade/yin-wave1-for-yang.md","content":"# YIN's wave-one findings (relayed to YANG for the trade)\nParaphrased faithfully from YIN's report; every number is YIN's measurement, not mine.\n\n## Shape\n65 non-test tools, 59 tool tests, 39 invariants, 445 + 168 node:test declarations, 82 package\nscripts (49 gates, 33 non-gates), 20 corpus/*.txt, only 6 `# checks:` machine-readable twins across\n3 of those 20, 76+11(+7 attic) assertion fixtures, 1305 assertion lines asserting 415 distinct\nscopes, 40 snapshots carrying 737 distinct scopes, 13 edition tiddlers (all with a reader).\n\n## Duplicate-intent pairs YIN names with evidence\nD1 — `swallow-witness` ⊂ `still`, BY THE AUTHOR'S OWN WORDS: still.js:35-38 — \"Pointed at ./corpus\nthis pass found 8 classes, every one already named, and swallow-witness finds the same 8 over the\nsame files with the same comparison.\" Same sentinel, carrier-reading, region-kind, ledger. still\nalready takes `--over <dir>`. Differences: swallow cuts every line and writes\nunasked-regions-ceiling; still samples unless --reach.\nD2 — bleed-canary vs corpus-check containment: both append a provocation and assert it takes only its\nown scopes; THREE different sentinel strings (two local consts plus the shared sentinel.js), and two\ndifferent baseline derivations (oracle `readAt().kind === 'built'` vs writing a control file).\nD3 — theme-parity, dark-construct and contrast-witness carry the SAME provenance anecdote nearly\nverbatim (a heading coloured in 9 of 65 themes while every gate read green).\nD4 — SIX independent readings of the `/^OWED/` prefix at five instrument sites; three strip the\n`READER <version>` prefix first, and `bracket-witness.js` and `light-cone.js` DO NOT — so the day a\n`READER <v> OWED` row lands in swallow-ledger or bracket-ledger, swallow reads it owed and light-cone\nreads it ruled, and light-cone's own gate goes quiet on it. 76 live `READER … OWED` rows today, all\nin darkness-ledger.\nD5 — judgements live in TWO homes: 20 corpus/*.txt and 9 JSON data tiddlers; colour-witness reads\none of each.\nD6 — three tools wearing a flag account for six gates (engine/behaviour, still/reach,\noverreach-host/cut). D7 — snap-tid and snap-meta are one tool, one scope, two globs.\nD8 — a duplication the house's own ward CANNOT SEE: one-implementation.test.js filters out\n`*.test.js`, and inside that blind spot sit a byte-identical `scopesOn` helper in two invariants and\n`source ./grammars.sh` inlined in two more — the exact work tokenizer.js holds.\n\n## Vocabulary drifts\nV1 file-kind suffix: 12 ledger-shaped files, only 10 named `-ledger`; expected-divergence and\nmust-fail are unsuffixed ledgers; 7 single-number ratchets split 4 floor / 3 ceiling, and\n`attribute-kind-ceiling` holds a count that may FALL while `coverage-floor` holds one that may RISE —\nthe filename encodes direction and gets it wrong once. colour-pair exists as both a ledger and a floor.\nV2 three spellings of over-reading (OVERREACH / overbound / overreach).\nV3 `MISS` is a HOMONYM across two ledgers that share one codec (line-grain dark vs character-grain\nunmarked).\nV4 four words for one lifecycle: stale / explains nothing / retires against `unruled` which names the\nopposite side; `idle` already exists in divergence-staleness and has not won.\nV5 eight reason prefixes; only HOST and READER have a shared reader.\nV6 444 `punctuation.definition` against 63 `punctuation.separator` and 8 `punctuation.section`, with\nSCOPE-NAMES ruling nothing about which sub-family a mark takes.\n\n## Record duplications\nR1 the migration headline exists in four places; the weld holds three hand-written restatement\nregexes; TWO further restatements say 111 where the certified number is 110 (MIGRATION:36,\nSCOPE-NAMES:20) — inside welded files. R2 LEDGER:1294 states 585/122/247 against the certified\n556/110/245. R3 \"65 bundled themes\" stated across 8 files, welded nowhere. R4 contrast-witness's\n`BAR = 16` is a literal while the ledger's prose derives it as a quarter of 65. R5 only 6 numbers in\nthe whole record carry a machine twin, none in the LEDGER's 1840 lines. R6 the README's gate list is\na hand enumeration: 25 distinct names, 3 duplicated bullets, 37 of the 49 gates unnamed, and the weld\nonly checks that a named script exists. R7 GateReport-Doc.tid says \"Seventeen instruments stand in\ntools/\" while gate-report.js's own header says the manifest counts them. R8 two differently-keyed\nenumerations of what is not a gate (a name-prefix regex and a reasons list) — and the regex form\nalready hid two CI instruments once.\n\n## L-Prime and archaeology, as counts\nCopulas per line: docs/scope-naming-prior-art.mem 0.17 (but 84 of its 87 sit inside a VERBATIM\nhandback — an L-Prime pass there would destroy the \"verbatim\" claim), LEDGER 0.07 (127 total,\ndominated by explanatory tails: \"which is\", \"is the\", \"is what\"), README/MIGRATION/CHANGELOG\n0.04-0.06, contributing.md ZERO. Archaeology: the RECORD is far more evergreen than the harness\nCOMMENTS; concentrations in gate-report.js:18-25 (a removed flag narrated in 8 lines),\ncoverage-floor (13 of 24 lines narrating two re-seats), ruling-breadth-ceiling, must-fail.\nFOUR stale present-tense counts that assert a blast radius and get it wrong: corpus-ledgers.test.js\n\"Thirteen\" (20), GateReport-Doc \"Seventeen\" (49/65), theme-model.test.js \"Four gates\" (12 requirers),\ntokenizer.test.js \"Twenty-two instruments\" (26).\n\n## Dead and aliased\nDead: `echo-test`, `list-test`, `run_snapshots.sh` (19 lines at the root, referenced by nothing but\nitself; snapshot-check.js does the work; no ward can see it). Aliased/narrowing: tests-advanced,\ntests-basic, tests-htmltiddler, tests-wikitext. Refuted collapse candidates kept: still-breadth.js and\ntw5-oracle-path.js look unreferenced but run as child processes inside swapped-grammar sandboxes.\nCI: the `compose` job duplicates what the `gates` job already runs — an exact duplicate job.\n\n## Where YIN suspects a collapse would LOSE something and cannot prove it — YOUR seam\nA. 50 of 87 fixtures assert no scope vocabulary a snapshot does not already carry — but the measure is\n   VOCABULARY, not scope-at-position, and a fixture pins intent with the law written beside it. YIN\n   says which of the 50 carry a law is YANG's to rule.\nB. The colour cluster: nine gates, each header distinguishing itself from its neighbours with a\n   number YIN did not re-run.\nC. overreach ×4: whether tests/samples/*.tw surfaces any class corpus/**/*.tw does not — unmeasured,\n   and LEDGER:1352 warns the shape exists in the other direction.\nD. The three flag-pairs and the two-glob pair: trivially cheap to fuse, but the harvest keys on each\n   gate's own summary line and the report reads \"49 of 49\".\nE. carrier-ledger vs swallow-ledger: identical row grammar; carrier-ledger refuses the fusion in its\n   own words; YIN could not confirm all 7 carrier rows lack a corpus specimen.\nF. prose-reading-ledger vs PlainConstructs: two homes, one shape; the stated distinction is real in\n   the instruments but YIN did not verify the two populations are disjoint.\nG. unasked-regions-ceiling vs swallow-ledger: coverage against correctness; the 97-region population\n   unconfirmed.\nH. The debt backlogs: ablation-ledger 330 of 359 rows OWED, darkness-ledger 93 of 111. Whether these\n   are enumerated backlogs or guards that stopped guarding decides the fate of the two largest corpus\n   files. YIN did not read the 423 reasons.\nI. syntaxes/attic SHIPS: .vscodeignore names no syntaxes/attic and package-contents checks manifest →\n   package only, never package → needed, so a 14KB dead sketch grammar rides into every install.\n   Inferred from source, NOT confirmed by building a .vsix.\nJ. 63 `punctuation.separator` sites unread; either a fifth unstated naming law exists or it is accretion.\n\n## YIN's ranked collapse list (17 items, in order)\n1 delete run_snapshots.sh + echo-test + list-test · 2 retire four narrowing test aliases ·\n3 one `owedOf()` beside `readerOf()` · 4 the byte-identical helper and the inlined grammars.sh, AND\nlift one-implementation's `.test.js` exclusion · 5 snap-tid + snap-meta · 6 drop the duplicate CI\ncompose job · 7 one home for the migration headline (fixes two wrong 111s) · 8 derive 65 and BAR ·\n9 generate the README gate list's completeness check, keep the curated prose · 10 fix the four stale\npresent-tense counts · 11 swallow-witness ⊂ still --over --reach (HIGHEST RISK; do not attempt\nwithout re-running both) · 12 three sentinels into one module · 13 corpus file naming to\n-ledger/-ratchet with direction in the first comment · 14 MISS → dark/unmarked · 15 one lifecycle\nvocabulary (idle/unruled/retired) · 16 move gate-report's archaeology paragraph into the LEDGER ·\n17 keep syntaxes/attic out of the .vsix (verify by building one first).\n","numLines":114,"startLine":1,"totalLines":114}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3a5dbb18-02ce-4132-93c6-faf6bbe583f4","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/VSCode-TW5-Syntax","sessionId":"7bdba225-5131-4cfb-a258-6d3e7da875f9","version":"2.1.277","gitBranch":"release/3.0.0","slug":"luminous-strolling-torvalds"}
