oes\n20\t   not use. CI's dirty-tree guard runs in the `grammar` job, not the `gates` job.\n21\t3. `every-test-runs` collects only `*.test.js` and only reads scripts matching `node --test`, so all\n22\t   96 assertion fixtures stand outside it — including 6 attic fixtures no glob reaches, deliberate\n23\t   but held by a README alone.\n24\t4. Four CI gates (`edition:check`, `lint-closure`, `package-contents`, `tests-known-gaps`) stand\n25\t   outside `every-gate-collides`. `package-contents.js` is a blocking CI gate with NO test file and\n26\t   no collider, and is the sole reader of \".vsix contents versus the manifest\".\n27\t5. 25 of 39 invariants show no collision marker at all, and NO ruling anywhere records that the\n28\t   invariants are exempt from the collider requirement.\n29\t\n30\t## The coupling a collapse must not break (YANG's strongest measurement)\n31\tPer-arm exclusive rulings over the 111: `overreach` 31 · `overreach-corpus-files` 57 ·\n32\t`overreach-corpus-memetic` 2 · `overreach-host` 2 · `overreach-cut` 0 · union 101 · unused 10.\n33\t`divergence-staleness` derives its run set FROM THE MANIFEST and calls a ruling stale only when it\n34\texplains nothing in the UNION. Fusing an arm therefore marks that arm's exclusives stale, and stale\n35\trulings get retired. Fusing the dialect arm retires the ruling that makes the dialect readable.\n36\tThe 10 unused rulings are exactly the 10 `READER 5.5.0-prerelease` ones; the gate reads green only\n37\tbecause `reader-scope.js` keys them out. 23 READER-tagged rulings: 12 at 5.4.1, 10 at\n38\t5.5.0-prerelease, 4 of those OWED.\n39\t\n40\t## Do-not-fuse pairs YANG defends with an axis\n41\tmodel vs engine (theme-model vs theme-collision — the only reader of what vscode-textmate paints);\n42\tscope-can-appear vs grammar-reachability vs corpus-check coverage (three causes of \"nothing reaches\n43\tit\"); dark-construct vs contrast-witness vs theme-parity (absent rule / quiet rule / below the\n44\tpanel median); five containment grains (bleed-canary / composition-check / swallow-witness /\n45\tmemetic-containment / corpus-check); six coverage authorities; engine-witness vs engine-behaviour\n46\t(1 ruling in engine-ledger, BEHAVIOUR-prefixed, filtered out of the compile arm); still vs\n47\tstill-reach (sampled vs whole: seeds 1,2,9,13 green and seed 5 red off one unchanged tree);\n48\trecord-vs-tree (MIGRATION gate-checked, README read as instruction not record).\n49\t\n50\t## Blind spots YANG ranks\n51\twithin-construct distinctness (deferred BY RULING, LEDGER:856-861 — do not let a collapse \"fix\" it\n52\tor delete the row); theme population hardcoded to node_modules/tm-themes in five instruments with no\n53\toverride, and the operator's own gruvbox is not among them; 106 figures of N/65-or-percent in the\n54\tLEDGER with two welds and zero coverage, both welds reading the UNRELEASED section only so they go\n55\tblind the day 3.1.0 opens; continuity unread by any instrument — the uri-span scouts are its only\n56\timplementation; 6 attic fixtures invisible; the gates job writing tracked files.\n57\t\n58\t## YANG's 19 load-bearing-prose sites (a comment or row is the only thing holding a law)\n59\tLEDGER 856-861 (witness deferred), 851-855 (fragment unarticulated), 780-790 (underline one stroke),\n60\t836-850 (two refused palette moves); tests/memetic-wikitext/attic/README.md; syntaxes/attic/README.md;\n61\tcorpus-ledgers.test.js header (\"Thirteen\" vs 20); a-lar-uri-reads-without-underline header;\n62\tgate-report.js 20-26 (the refuted --in-process spike) and 38-46 (reader-keyed report routing, held by\n63\tno test) and its SKIP regex; coverage-floor, ruling-breadth-ceiling, carrier-reach-floor,\n64\tlegibility-floor, colour-pair-ledger headers; backtrack-witness.test.js 48-66; CI test.yml 60-69\n65\t(dirty-tree guard reason) and 88-95 — the ruling that re-running four gates in the blocking job is\n66\tNOT redundancy but the thing that makes them blocking. A YIN pass reading that as duplication would\n67\tsilently un-block four gates.\n68\t\n69\t## Fragile set\n70\tTwo gates write tracked files (above). backtrack-witness is wall-clock: 1.4ms alone vs past 8ms under\n71\tthe suite on identical bytes; 0 stalls vs 6 between two runs at rest. still --sample 25 is\n72\tdraw-dependent. Conditional skips read as passes on machines lacking a checkout/seed/plugin.\n73\tSeveral instruments change POPULATION on a flag, so fusing arms picks one population permanently.\n74\t\n75\t## Where YANG suspects redundancy and cannot prove it — YOUR seam\n76\t1. `snap-tid` + `snap-meta` — same scope, populations 2 and 1. Weakest defence of any gate.\n77\t2. `overreach-cut` — 0 exclusive rulings, defended only by `degraded-ground.test.js`'s header.\n78\t3. dark-construct vs contrast-witness — finding overlap UNMEASURED; YANG says this one is YIN's to\n79\t   settle and it will take the measurement.\n80\t4. canary-tid (2 files) and canary-memetic (4) — what canary-memetic catches that\n81\t   memetic-containment does not, unmeasured.\n82\t5. theme-paint / family-atlas / page-palette / reading-recipe — CLI surfaces may merge; their\n83\t   QUESTIONS may not. page-palette's question is read by nothing else.\n84\t6. uri-span-measure / uri-span-compare — look like dead code, are the only implementation of the\n85\t   continuity reading and are cited by name as the evidence for the operator's underline ruling.\n86\t7. The shared modules (sentinel, region-kind, carrier-reading, ledger-shape, walk, jsonc, tokenizer,\n87\t   run-tool, still-breadth, tw5-oracle-path) — each header records the drift it prevents; they are\n88\t   the RESULTS of earlier collapses. one-implementation catches a re-expansion but not a wrong fusion.\n89\t"}]},"uuid":"cfb5060c-583a-4993-9048-fe32b9fe5977","timestamp":"2026-10-07T16:32:20.798Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/joshu/.claude/jobs/86a17260/tmp/trade/yang-wave1-for-yin.md","content":"# YANG's wave-one findings (relayed to YIN for the trade)\nParaphrased faithfully from YANG's report; every number is YANG's measurement, not mine.\n\n## Shape\n49 gates over 35 distinct instruments — 14 gates are one tool under different arguments.\n19 tool-shaped npm scripts excluded from the gate list by the SKIP regex. 39 invariants.\n20 corpus ledger/floor/ceiling files. 111 rulings in expected-divergence. 65 themes. 40 snapshots.\n96 assertion fixtures (76 .tw5.test, 11 .mem.test, 6 attic, 2 known-gaps, 1 in samples).\n\n## Faults YANG found in the verifier itself\n1. `every-gate-collides` has a MEASURED FALSE GREEN. It matches a gate's NAME against RAW text and\n   its collider CLAUSE against comment-stripped code, so both halves can be satisfied by different\n   parts of one file. For `theme-collision` the only qualifying file is `theme-model.test.js`, which\n   names the tool ONLY in a line-4 comment. Deleting that comment reds a genuinely collided gate;\n   deleting `theme-collision.test.js`'s real `--must-fail` arm keeps the invariant GREEN.\n   `corpus-ledgers.test.js` already strips comments before its name match, with the reason written.\n2. `gate-report --check` IS NOT READ-ONLY. Two of the 49 write tracked files on their manifest\n   invocation: `ceiling` (textmate-ceiling.js --write → TextMateCeiling.tid) and `builtins`\n   (builtins-sync.js with no --check → a syntaxes/*.json). Both have a --check arm the manifest does\n   not use. CI's dirty-tree guard runs in the `grammar` job, not the `gates` job.\n3. `every-test-runs` collects only `*.test.js` and only reads scripts matching `node --test`, so all\n   96 assertion fixtures stand outside it — including 6 attic fixtures no glob reaches, deliberate\n   but held by a README alone.\n4. Four CI gates (`edition:check`, `lint-closure`, `package-contents`, `tests-known-gaps`) stand\n   outside `every-gate-collides`. `package-contents.js` is a blocking CI gate with NO test file and\n   no collider, and is the sole reader of \".vsix contents versus the manifest\".\n5. 25 of 39 invariants show no collision marker at all, and NO ruling anywhere records that the\n   invariants are exempt from the collider requirement.\n\n## The coupling a collapse must not break (YANG's strongest measurement)\nPer-arm exclusive rulings over the 111: `overreach` 31 · `overreach-corpus-files` 57 ·\n`overreach-corpus-memetic` 2 · `overreach-host` 2 · `overreach-cut` 0 · union 101 · unused 10.\n`divergence-staleness` derives its run set FROM THE MANIFEST and calls a ruling stale only when it\nexplains nothing in the UNION. Fusing an arm therefore marks that arm's exclusives stale, and stale\nrulings get retired. Fusing the dialect arm retires the ruling that makes the dialect readable.\nThe 10 unused rulings are exactly the 10 `READER 5.5.0-prerelease` ones; the gate reads green only\nbecause `reader-scope.js` keys them out. 23 READER-tagged rulings: 12 at 5.4.1, 10 at\n5.5.0-prerelease, 4 of those OWED.\n\n## Do-not-fuse pairs YANG defends with an axis\nmodel vs engine (theme-model vs theme-collision — the only reader of what vscode-textmate paints);\nscope-can-appear vs grammar-reachability vs corpus-check coverage (three causes of \"nothing reaches\nit\"); dark-construct vs contrast-witness vs theme-parity (absent rule / quiet rule / below the\npanel median); five containment grains (bleed-canary / composition-check / swallow-witness /\nmemetic-containment / corpus-check); six coverage authorities; engine-witness vs engine-behaviour\n(1 ruling in engine-ledger, BEHAVIOUR-prefixed, filtered out of the compile arm); still vs\nstill-reach (sampled vs whole: seeds 1,2,9,13 green and seed 5 red off one unchanged tree);\nrecord-vs-tree (MIGRATION gate-checked, README read as instruction not record).\n\n## Blind spots YANG ranks\nwithin-construct distinctness (deferred BY RULING, LEDGER:856-861 — do not let a collapse \"fix\" it\nor delete the row); theme population hardcoded to node_modules/tm-themes in five instruments with no\noverride, and the operator's own gruvbox is not among them; 106 figures of N/65-or-percent in the\nLEDGER with two welds and zero coverage, both welds reading the UNRELEASED section only so they go\nblind the day 3.1.0 opens; continuity unread by any instrument — the uri-span scouts are its only\nimplementation; 6 attic fixtures invisible; the gates job writing tracked files.\n\n## YANG's 19 load-bearing-prose sites (a comment or row is the only thing holding a law)\nLEDGER 856-861 (witness deferred), 851-855 (fragment unarticulated), 780-790 (underline one stroke),\n836-850 (two refused palette moves); tests/memetic-wikitext/attic/README.md; syntaxes/attic/README.md;\ncorpus-ledgers.test.js header (\"Thirteen\" vs 20); a-lar-uri-reads-without-underline header;\ngate-report.js 20-26 (the refuted --in-process spike) and 38-46 (reader-keyed report routing, held by\nno test) and its SKIP regex; coverage-floor, ruling-breadth-ceiling, carrier-reach-floor,\nlegibility-floor, colour-pair-ledger headers; backtrack-witness.test.js 48-66; CI test.yml 60-69\n(dirty-tree guard reason) and 88-95 — the ruling that re-running four gates in the blocking job is\nNOT redundancy but the thing that makes them blocking. A YIN pass reading that as duplication would\nsilently un-block four gates.\n\n## Fragile set\nTwo gates write tracked files (above). backtrack-witness is wall-clock: 1.4ms alone vs past 8ms under\nthe suite on identical bytes; 0 stalls vs 6 between two runs at rest. still --sample 25 is\ndraw-dependent. Conditional skips read as passes on machines lacking a checkout/seed/plugin.\nSeveral instruments change POPULATION on a flag, so fusing arms picks one population permanently.\n\n## Where YANG suspects redundancy and cannot prove it — YOUR seam\n1. `snap-tid` + `snap-meta` — same scope, populations 2 and 1. Weakest defence of any gate.\n2. `overreach-cut` — 0 exclusive rulings, defended only by `degraded-ground.test.js`'s header.\n3. dark-construct vs contrast-witness — finding overlap UNMEASURED; YANG says this one is YIN's to\n   settle and it will take the measurement.\n4. canary-tid (2 files) and canary-memetic (4) — what canary-memetic catches that\n   memetic-containment does not, unmeasured.\n5. theme-paint / family-atlas / page-palette / reading-recipe — CLI surfaces may merge; their\n   QUESTIONS may not. page-palette's question is read by nothing else.\n6. uri-span-measure / uri-span-compare — look like dead code, are the only implementation of the\n   continuity reading and are cited by name as the evidence for the operator's underline ruling.\n7. The shared modules (sentinel, region-kind, carrier-reading, ledger-shape, walk, jsonc, tokenizer,\n   run-tool, still-breadth, tw5-oracle-path) — each header records the drift it prevents; they are\n   the RESULTS of earlier collapses. one-implementation catches a re-expansion but not a wrong fusion.\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e98a4e54-e71c-4aa5-a1d0-1e43f024bf03","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/VSCode-TW5-Syntax","sessionId":"7bdba225-5131-4cfb-a258-6d3e7da875f9","version":"2.1.277","gitBranch":"release/3.0.0","slug":"luminous-strolling-torvalds"}
