eside the instrument it collides, and holding a\ntest to the no-second-implementation rule would FORBID the collision the house requires.\nRULING: CONDITIONAL — keep the exclusion, extend the existing named-exemption mechanism to the\nfingerprint scan.\nDuplications measured: the byte-identical `scopesOn` helper exists in exactly TWO invariants (YIN's\ncount right); a THIRD file carries a function of the same name that is a different function\n(offset-based, returns an array) — a legibility hazard nothing reads. `source ./grammars.sh` is\ninlined ONCE, not twice (the second file YIN named reads grammars.sh as a file, a different act).\nSo lifting the exclusion surfaces two real duplications — both fixable today without touching the ward.\n\n## A5 The debt backlogs: CONCEDED, with a structural condition\nRead EVERY owed reason in both files (not a sample). ablation-ledger: 359 rows, 319 OWED, **22 distinct\nreason bodies**, distinct stems also 22 — byte-identical repeats, largest family 96 rows (a style run's\n`;`/`:` separators), then 40, 38, 38, 23, 18, 14, 10. darkness-ledger: 111 rows, 92 OWED, **5 distinct\nbodies**, 3 distinct stems, largest family 89 rows (a filter or template-title value spanning a blank\nline) — and that cause is stated a second time in the file's own header.\nRULING: these are not 319 and 92 guards; they are 22 and 5 causes enumerated at the row granularity the\nkey grammar forces (one row per character position).\nCONDITION, non-negotiable: a single-number ratchet seated at 1 refuses a ruling absorbing more than one\ncause, and its header records why — a predecessor ratchet on corpus-token share re-seated four times in\none session (55.8 → 56.6 → 57.2 → 60.0%), every reason true, because authoring more of what is already\nruled raises the share. So the collapse is safe ONLY once the ledger row grammar carries a `cause`\nidentifier distinct from its `key` and the breadth ratchet counts distinct causes rather than keys.\nThen ~400 lines of verbatim repetition leave the two largest ledgers and nothing is lost — the single\nlargest honest reduction on either list.\n\n## Part B verdicts on YIN's candidates\nsnap-tid + snap-meta — CONCEDE, nothing lost (2 and 1 sample files; a different invariant holds the\nfile associations).\noverreach-cut — CONDITIONAL, and the condition is CI, not the gate: `degraded-ground.test.js` runs the\ncut arm itself with a byte-identical invocation, but it SKIPS unless a TiddlyWiki checkout sits as a\nSIBLING of the repository — true on the operator's machine, false in CI. So in CI the gate is the only\nreader of degraded ground. Fix the test's host resolution first, then the gate can go.\nengine-witness / engine-behaviour — DEFEND (a compile is not an agreement; the engine ledger's single\nruling is BEHAVIOUR-prefixed and filtered out of the compile arm).\nstill / still-reach — DEFEND (sampled vs whole; the carrier floor seated at 0.9947; 23 of 4,403\ncarriers hold an unnamed class so a draw of 25 misses all 23 seven times in eight; seeds 1/2/9/13 green\nand seed 5 red off one unchanged tree).\nThe harvest's per-arm summary line is HABIT: the report counts what the manifest names and no file\nstates 49.\nrun_snapshots.sh + echo-test + list-test — CONCEDE all three, with a coupling: run_snapshots.sh is\nreferenced once more, by `.vscodeignore:16`, and the package gate checks manifest→package only, so a\nstale ignore entry would go unreported. Delete both lines together.\nThe four stale present-tense counts — ALL FOUR CONFIRMED: theme-model's \"Four gates\" against 12\nnon-test readers (8 of them gates, 18 requirers total); tokenizer's \"Twenty-two\" against 26 non-test\n(35 total); the doc tiddler's \"Seventeen instruments\" against 49 gates over 35 instruments — while the\ntool's own header refuses to state a count; the corpus-ledger invariant's \"Thirteen\" against 20.\n\n## Part C — YANG's verdict over YIN's 17, plus ordering\nCONCEDE: 1, 2, 3 (promoted to FIRST), 4a, 5, 6, 7 (a correctness fix — two restatements say 111 where\nthe certified figure is 110, and one file contradicts itself 31 lines apart), 8 (and WIDEN), 9, 10,\n12 (strings only), 13, 14, 15.\nDEFEND / CONDITIONAL: 4b (decline as written; extend the exemption map instead), 11 (defend — the\nswallow witness alone computes a coverage ceiling seated at 14 over a population of 97 regions, with\n83 standing open under some cut and agreeing with the host; adding 800 upstream carriers opens twelve\nmore), 16 (move, never lose — and carry the reader-keyed report routing note with it, which no test\nholds), 17 (verify by building a .vsix first; same missing package→needed direction as item 1).\nYANG's own items YIN did not touch: the collider invariant's false green (name matched in a comment,\nclause matched elsewhere; the real collider is excellent and invisible — one-line fix, strip comments\nbefore the name match); two of the 49 gates writing tracked files so the report is not read-only;\nfour CI-blocking instruments outside the collider requirement, one with no test at all; nothing\ncollides the 39 invariants and no ruling says why; the deliberate absences (the within-construct\nwitness, the unarticulated fragment) and the two throwaway scouts that are the only implementation of\nthe continuity reading — all of which look exactly like gaps and dead code and are neither.\n\n## THE BLIND SPOT YIN MADE VISIBLE TO YANG\nThe record and the harness have NO SYNTAX for \"this number was true when measured\" versus \"this number\nis true now\", and every staleness finding in both reports is downstream of that one absence. Arrived at\nfrom four directions: a ledger row stating 585/122/247 against the certified 556/110/245 while\nnarrating a sequence; two restatements saying 111 for 110 in welded files in shapes the weld's patterns\ndo not match; 106 figures of N-of-65 or a percentage in the welded section with ZERO read by anything\nand only 6 machine-readable twins in the whole repository; and three harness doc-comment derivations\nthat reproduce in rank and ratio but not in integer.\nCURE, one mark: a dated reading carries its date, a live claim carries a machine-readable twin, and a\nfigure carrying neither fails its gate. That single distinction retires YIN's items 7, 8 and 10 and\nYANG's wave-one staleness class at once — the only item on either list that pays for itself across\nboth the record and the harness.\n\n## Ordering advice\nItem 3 first (the only latent fault that disarms a gate). The dated-reading mark second (retires four\nitems). Then 1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 10, 13, 14, 15, 4a freely. Hold 11 and 17 for measurement. Decline 4b as\nwritten.\n\n## Not verified\nNo .vsix built · no gate report, tool suite, backtrack, snapshot, canary or theme gate run (gates\nactually run across both waves: the five overreach arms and divergence-staleness) · three doc-comment\nintegers not reproducible (claimed only as not-reproducible, not as wrong) · two OWED counting methods\ndiffer (330/93 by line grep, 319/92 by reason-splitting; the distinct-reason counts 22 and 5 are robust\nto that) · YIN's attic fixture count (7 vs 6), node:test declaration counts, copula densities and the\ntwo sandbox probe claims unverified.\n","numLines":149,"startLine":1,"totalLines":149}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3602bbc2-e943-401f-889e-65913be155c3","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/VSCode-TW5-Syntax","sessionId":"7bdba225-5131-4cfb-a258-6d3e7da875f9","version":"2.1.277","gitBranch":"release/3.0.0","slug":"luminous-strolling-torvalds"}
