/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/packages/lararium-node/probes/crossing-roles.ts:67:  server.stand({ gate: stood.gate, pin: stood.pin });
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor.mem:141:''The island-door inventory measures reach, never policy.'' `tools/capability-inventory-witness.sh` reads, on the built tree, which of the four vessel doors (fetch, rest, custody write, dyad) each island class reaches, against the committed table `tools/capability-inventory.json`. A cell answers one question: does an ask from that class arrive at a door at all. On node every door stands as a stand-in that grants every ask and counts each call; what the real door then answers a real ask, a miss, a refusal or `aside`, stays outside the table. Each row drives the real code that builds its class's handle: a pool's own host spawn for the wiki and session islands, on node, and over a stand-in Web Worker in the browser, where the row reads every reply and counts the listeners the spawn attached. A row the tool cannot drive whole outside a browser reads `unmeasured` in every cell, never `silent`; the browser's daemon island reads so, since its spawn seam stands inside the vessel's open. A session island's view asks run through the pool's own listener, which no row drives: on node the content its view passes ends at the fetch door, behind that view's gate. Two source readings hold what no row drives, each counted per occurrence within a file: every reference to a function that spawns, wraps or answers an island, with every raw worker constructor and every renamed import of one, and every quoted ask or answer type of the doors and the view.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:67:# ''Every boot rests at the floor.'' A verb that needs sovereign state refuses at a standing floor and names `lares vault unlock`. A harness that reads the first `gate key:` line of a log reads the carriage relay's key where a relay stands.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:184:* ''Removal's reach'': four edges take a marker (dyad, vouch, member, carriage). A vouch edge answers to its voucher and to a chartered quorum; a seal roll carries every shadow; a standing shadow reaches every gate and drives a key roll; a contested tie keeps the shadow up; mutual removal ends in an explicit fork (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:195:* ''The system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Only each Nexus's Kahu cabal writes the `lares` and `lararium` wikis and bags live. Every other wiki, and every other hand, mounts them read-only by CID: the latest release that cabal approved. The release rides the Nexus's crossroads board as its public answer, naming the floor CID under the Kahu steward's seal. The cabal approves the exact bytes under its charter's threshold, and a herm carries the answer without signing it. Every wiki mounts that floor through `@oracle`, which never writes. A vessel moves its floor pin only when it accepts a newer signed release. With no Nexus speaking, it stands on its last accepted floor, or on genesis. A face's wikis follow the floor of the Nexus that face stands in, so one vessel may hold two floors and never ties its faces together. An edit aimed at the floor copies up into the wiki's own working layer, and an offering back travels as a draft into the cabal's realm. A lone hearth is a Nexus of one, so its operator stands as its own Kahu. Row `W26` carries the build.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:203:* ''One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above them'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"it's the only way to retain control over faces that don't know about each other"//). Each face's PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, its event store, its registry, its archive and its content-key seat; no vessel-wide identity registers a face's bags, delegates them, or holds a face's group. Two faces of one vessel then never link on the wire, a removal from one face rolls that face's bags alone, and a bundle restores one face and nothing of another. Today the vessel's own identity registers every bag and delegates each face's bags through itself, and the vessel and every face share one event store and one content-key holder (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/keyhive-per-persona-group-2026">>). House readings under the operator's confidence, each naming what flips it: a herm keeps a floor-only transport key, behind a red test that it can neither author, resolve nor observe a face's capabilities, and holds no Keyhive identity if that test fails; several face hives share one process only after a substrate probe reads them isolated, and each face's hive runs in its own worker otherwise; co-mingled history migrates by fresh identities and an old mixed archive refuses by name, with no bridge; a founder that cannot leave its group leaves by a fresh PersonaGroup. Row `K15` carries the build, folding `W25` and `K12`; `W26`'s slice 3 waits on its face context.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:211:* ''Each realm stands under one charter, a seed's or a Nexus's'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18). A council that meets at one hearth stands under that hearth's seed charter, and its guests' chosen faces walk there with no Nexus founded; a council two hearths carry stands under the Nexus those two found fresh, since a Nexus names the operators' relationship (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae">> #/edge-hands). A guest sees every realm its worn face stands in.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:219:* ''The ember's serving gate'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A third gate tier, the serving route, takes its bundle from SK, and the floor and sovereign tiers stand untouched; a pin moves only by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step, and no quiet period ages a pin out. The reason: a dialer that pinned the sovereign tier never mistakes a serving hearth for an unlocked one. The ruling flips on proof that a gate pin decides no authority anywhere (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:230:* ''Engine cadence'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Cadence keeps its own lineage and threshold, apart from every seat key. A Nexus's joint founding cites one cadence inception that names each founder's hearth, the device that bears the reboot, as a holder; a household seed carries none, since its one holder bears its reboots. Each hearth mints its cadence key at random on the device, never derived from serving or floor material, and keeps it, with its next-key commitment, as a `cold` row under the vessel key that unwraps per act; no sixth custody class and no extra card at the founding. A holder may later rotate onto a cold card by its own choice. Each island pins one engine epoch, and one daemon hosts two epochs only as two separately pinned islands. The reason: the people who bear a reboot decide it, and a seat-holder who runs no hardware forces no one's restart. The ruling flips on a cadence act that must run unattended where a per-act unwrap cannot (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:232:* ''A restore after guardian enrolment'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A face's own bundle restores after it enrols guardians, so long as the face's log still holds the set its own root enrolled by the typed first event and no later event moved it; a guardian rotation that moves the set cuts every earlier bundle off. The restored face stands provisional as the restore's key-history ruling holds. The reason: enrolling guardians must never silently kill a person's own backups, and the guardians' rotation, not the enrolment, cuts off a stolen bundle. The ruling flips on a provisional gate that cannot stop a restored face from signing an authority-changing act before a party confirms it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:237:* ''The admit's gate pin'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). The admit carriage and fleet-join answer sign a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at the named Nexus, read by `readGateBundlePin`; its digest derives from that object. Dials index by (hearth, Nexus, route, tier). Floor routes receive their own full pins through an authenticated relation or a carried signed pin set; an announcement never authenticates its own first pin. The reason: a digest alone gives an offline dialer no trusted route or key. The ruling flips on an equally authenticated digest-to-full-pin carrier with an unambiguous route and offline first contact.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:248:* ''The channel of intent'' (operator, 2026-10-20: //"Approve your leans, land the full models into the architecture now"//). The daemon wiki keeps working memory; a face's intents travel on that face's own intent plane, `@intents-<tag>`, a fifth face plane beside the four; a vessel's own records rest in its daemon bag, unmirrored; the face's pins rest in the face's custody and `@persona`. The approved leans: the plane stands from the first landing, never staged in the daemon bag; the winner reads by the intent's own preference list, else the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, and never elects; a single-effect fleet-wide verb never addresses "any device", and a human answer may name its executor; a claim never expires, a device's staleness stays a local suspicion, and the operator's release always wins; an `every` intent reaches a later-joined device unless its bound names a roster edge; a far agent reaches the plane through a relay seat, opt-in per face and ring-gated, its research before its build; an intent voids by supersession, a revoked delegation, a passed roster edge or the operator's cancel; compaction folds by the operator's act, never a timer; a local verb that touches its own vessel alone bypasses the plane and leaves its receipt in that vessel's bag. The plane carries a hand's decisions that cross devices, never its motion (the rubric, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">> #/the-rubric). Row `I1`.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:274:* ''The multi-Nexus fold.'' A gate answers strangers if ANY Nexus it stands in reads OPEN. One gate key serves every Nexus a vessel carries, so this rule reduces exactly to per-Nexus posture once each Nexus carries its own wire key (R-WIRE) — not an interim.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:335:* ''The vessel-identity family'': the persona roster, the worn-face selector, the pet-name map, the declaration map and the published-face record rest sealed under the VK as hot rows; each persona root rests as a cold row, opened for one act; the floor vessel key rests beside its signed inception, every load proves that inception, and no next-key seed or commitment rides it. The roster commits a root: a mint writes the root row, then the roster line that carries the root's public key, so a reading of a public key answers off the hot roster and opens no root. A root row with no roster line reads as an orphan: no reader holds it, `lares persona list` names it, and the same mint run again adopts it. A roster line whose root row went missing, or names another key, refuses by name at the act that needs the seed, and nothing mints over it. A hot row with nothing at its path reads as holding nothing; a row that stands and does not open, or opens to another shape, refuses by name at every read and every write. A vessel key mints only inside a held custody, and lands with its inception under the custody's one claim: the key file commits the mint, so two acts never commit two keys, and a boot loads a key and never mints one. The floor reads no row of the family, so a carried-Nexus reading by persona (a seated chair, a kept consent) answers empty until the key arrives, and a sovereign composition reads the roster whole before it stands (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`). A floor composition reads no roster, so it shuts every fleet lane: it sorts every device as set aside, sets a proven sibling aside, and its fetch door reads no peer as fleet, the pinned join gate's key included (`packages/lararium-node/src/floor-fleet-lanes.ts`). It still folds the one fleet board its own device edge names in the clear, so the Binding Gate reads this vessel's own seat at every standing.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:338:* ''The hosting rows'': a hearth's hosting state, each spend and its walkers' carriage rest as HOT rows sealed under the VK, in the storage home of the custody seat (`packages/lararium-node/src/hosting-store.ts`, `hosting-carry.ts`). The sealed writer writes a whole file and appends to none, so each spend lands as ONE row of its own, named by a digest of its nonce or marker: the row's presence IS the burn, and it reads, decides and seals under one custody holder. The spend row commits a redemption, and what rides ahead of it re-derives: the grant from the epoch, the leaf, the nonce and the claim, so a crash before the answer replays as `retry`; the operator's counts from the rows standing, by name. A roll's state row commits the roll, and the hosting doc re-derives from it: the next roll and each sovereign stand land an act the sealed state holds and the doc lacks (`landHostingActs`). The sweep of dead epochs' rows passes through the seat's removal door (`removeCustodyRow`), which removes only a row this vessel's key opens; a spend that sealed after a roll retired its epoch burns nothing live and leaves with the next sweep. Each carried value rests as one row whose name carries its address and its length, so a guest's bytes read off its rows and no counter stands beside them. One process serves a hearth's carriage (the standing vessel's own gate, under its store claim), and its contacts and deposits run in turn, so a quota reads the bytes the last deposit left and a reclaim never discards on a reading a contact moved meanwhile. A row that stands and does not open refuses by name: a burn nobody can read never reads as unspent, and a carried value nobody can open never reads as absent. A floor composition reads no hosting row, so a locked hearth sorts no socket as a walker. `lares host`, `host roll` and `host invite` ride the custody door (`host.state` · `host.roll` · `host.invite`): a minted invite as a verb's outcome would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:341:* ''The gate's two root doors'' (specified in code; no composer calls them until the socket cutover): a floor gate's bundle derives through the floor key's door, which answers at a locked vessel, hands back a fresh child and never the floor key (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`); a sovereign gate's bundle derives through the custody seat's door, which answers only while the seat holds its key (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`). The doors carry two types, so no line swaps them by accident; a root refuses the other tier's door by name; each seat's door refuses the other tier's child; and a weld holds the two mints to the two seats (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:342:* ''The gate's memory rows'' (specified in code; no gate calls them until the socket cutover): a sovereign gate's withdrawal memory rests one row per face key in the vessel's storage home, named by the face's proof-subject digest and sealed under the VK, so a locked vessel's disk names no face key (`gate-memory` in the carrier table; `packages/lararium-node/src/gate-memory-rows.ts`). Each write reads, decides and seals under one custody holder, and refuses where it would drop an event the row holds; a locked seat refuses by name. An older copy of a row restored by hand makes a gate forget until the next honest vessel dials, and no fence stands against that hand. A row that stands and does not fold whole refuses by name and reports it (`GateMemoryRowTorn`): the asking gate falls silent, no keep writes over the row, and a person repairs it by hand, where a row read as nothing would let a fresh memory admit a vessel the row once denied. No backup bundle carries the row: a vessel that stands again knows nothing (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-withdrawal-proof">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:343:* ''The session and the boot'': the daemon stands at the floor holding no VK and unlocks on a custody frame of its owner-only socket (`unlock` · `lock` · `custody` · `act` · `backup`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-frames.ts`), handled ahead of every verb, so the credential the CLI reads on its TTY reaches no receipt, outcome or log. One holder keeps the opened VK in node-main (`custody-holder.ts`); an unlock tears the standing composition down and stands a fresh one on the same floor (`open-node-vessel.ts`), a lock returns it to the floor, and three failed unlocks spend a boot's attempts. A composition that refuses above the floor leaves the floor standing and names its fault once. The settle sweeps a sidecar whose write never landed. The test door (`tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs`) opens marked scratch roots alone, and the marker earns one loud line in `vault status` and the boot log. Every boot composes at the floor: nothing stored lifts it. A daemon island holds no VK, so its archive exports cross the custody write door (`custody:write`) and the main thread seals them. Every broad sync port, the daemon island's and each wiki island's, crosses one hardened facade on both ends: an arrival that reads as no sync message drops at the port and never reaches a listener that would throw on it (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-repo.ts`). The daemon island's gates ask the main thread what a device's edge reads on its fleet's board through the dyad door (`dyad:ask`), which answers `aside` wherever it cannot read. Each fold of the fleet's edge board sets off the key side's settle on an unlocked vessel, with no timer and no person: the main thread places the island's `seat-duties` verb, awaits its answer and keeps the signed rolls (`packages/lararium-node/src/seat-settle.ts`; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/what-the-code-holds">>). Those two doors and the rest door answer the daemon island's channel alone: each worker's class binds at its spawn (`packages/lararium-node/src/worker-handle.ts`), a wiki island reaches the fetch door alone while its custody write and its rest ask refuse by name and its dyad ask draws `aside`, and a session island reaches no vessel door. A command that acts with no vessel standing opens its own key session at the first sealed row it touches (`packages/lares-cli/src/offline-custody.ts`): a terminal prompt, and under a marked scratch root the published test route. A sealed row's act rides an `act` frame of the custody door and never a store verb: one typed table bounds the acts (`packages/lararium-node/src/sealed-acts.ts`), a standing vessel answers with no second prompt, and beside a standing vessel a command opens no key session of its own, while a root's recovery split refuses there (`packages/lares-cli/src/sealed-act-door.ts`). The fleet mirror of a pet-name and a declared Handle rides that door too: `selves.carry` names a face and which name, the vessel's main thread reads the name off its sealed row and writes it onto that face's own persona plane and no other face's, only where that plane's rest seals (a clear rest refuses the carry and the name stays on its row), `lares persona sync` fills and never replaces, and no verb takes or answers a face's own name (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:363:''R-CHARTER, the one AID train.'' Its first stage stands landed (train K of #/the-trains): the chairs sign with seat keys of their own and pre-rotate on cold cards, a Nexus answers to `nexus-<sha>`, the floor key commits no next key, per-Nexus keys mint at random, the PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, and the Stable founding act founds a hearth (`lares vessel found --hearth`): the place, persona zero and a PRIVATE seed charter at one seat, with no keyring, every fleet relation bound to that charter's AID, and every harness that founds a hearth founding through it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/found">>). What stays owed:
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:369:* A per-Nexus wire key in two tiers (operator ruling): a floor route's bundle derives from the floor key and answers at a locked vessel; a sovereign route's bundle derives from the sealed custody root and stands only while the vessel stands unlocked. One gate per (Nexus, route), so knock, pin, verdict and posture read per Nexus exactly (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). The serving route's third tier rides train E (`E3`).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:372:* One client dial per (hearth, Nexus), so a vessel walks at more than one hearth; until then a second walk hearth refuses aloud.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:385:* ''Working-layer law the build owes'': one working document per (face, wiki, slot kind); its address derives from a secret only that face's vessels hold. The working layer follows its wiki across recipe recomposition. A leaf with an admit and no seat writes nothing to face wikis until join completion. Vessel removal leaves the address standing; the gate and document membership refuse the removed vessel (operator ruling).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the VK included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. Wave D (the FCK fence, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) and `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) build beside each other; `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) follows Wave D.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:483:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
