   161	''The gate reads the header before any Noise work'' and refuses by name, each name drawing the same silence on the wire: `flight-absent`, `flight-overlong` (checked before the value splits), `flight-shape` (anything but two non-empty entries), `flight-protocol` (the first entry names anything but `lar-gate`, in its one case and order), `flight-token` (any character outside the alphabet, or a short token). List whitespace beside the comma reads as space and tab alone. The reader holds no memory: a replayed flight reads again and buys provisional work alone (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-exchange.ts`).
   162	
   163	''What the measurement read'' (one run, a house reading of its instruments): Chromium 156, Firefox 157 and WebKit 27.2 under Playwright 1.64, over plain sockets on loopback, direct and behind `nginx:1.30-alpine` under the household terminator's own settings.
   164	
   165	|! Reading |! Measured |
   166	| the header as sent | the list in the order given, joined by `, ` |
   167	| the alphabet | Chromium and Firefox refuse `=`, `/`, space and the other separators at construction; unpadded base64url passes in all three |
   168	| the bound, direct | every engine carried 196608 payload bytes; the browsers set no bound the envelope nears |
   169	| the bound, behind the terminator | a 16013-byte header passed; a 21859-byte header drew 400 before the upstream saw it |
   170	| the bound, behind stock nginx | an 8013-byte header passed; an 8205-byte header drew 400 |
   171	| an unanswered upgrade | Firefox closes it after 20 s; Chromium and WebKit still waited at 75 s |
   172	| the terminator's log | its stock access line keeps the request path, so it keeps the knock; no line keeps the token |
   173	
   174	''Unmeasured'': the envelope through TLS and through HTTP/2's extended CONNECT, on a phone's own engine, and behind a proxy other than nginx. One Android tablet carried 8192 payload bytes in this header (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/device-capabilities-2026">>).
