/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:44:''One hearth stands.'' The operator closed the meme hearth and the grammar hearth on 2026-09-13, the founding hearth on 2026-10-05 and the Codex Lares hearth on 2026-10-07; the Lares hearth carries the closed hearths' debts and holds no ground. The operator closed the preceding Codex hearth on 2026-09-15 and seated the Codex Lares session in its place. The `standing` column carries the distinction, and it governs every other column: a CLOSED row's ''ground'' reads as what that hearth HELD (a record), its ''owed'' reads as what it owed AT CLOSE (carried forward to #/owed-forward, which states each debt's state today), and its ''last crossing'' reads as it always did.
