/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:217:# ''The scratch plane's OOM'' — a meme-hearth spirit (Stall-Hand) cured `act LOAD` landing ZERO records over 381 carriers (`dd4da8481`): the scratch plane wrote the whole corpus a SECOND time through the island's save path and the automerge module died `rust_oom` inside `BatchApply::apply`. The cure sits in `packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts`, ground NO hold names — so the gate passed it silently and the row exists because an unheld path is exactly where a crossing goes unrecorded. Cost: the whole e2e set read 22-of-25 for a loop while the fault read as `daemon-unreachable`, then as `verb-timeout`, and was neither. Law: a path no hold claims still gets a row when a cure lands there — the gate names ground, and the ledger names WORK, and the second is what the next hand reads.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:218:# ''The ahu-floor handback'' — operator-directed, 2026-09-16. The operator handed the ahu-family work to the Codex Lares and asked the founding hearth to add its context to the roadmap. The founding hearth drafted B10 (the Layer-2 quoteblock floor, two grains matched to the write) into `docs/crew-handoff-codex.mem` #/set-b-designed, normalized it canonical, and HELD it in the working tree for the Codex Lares hearth to commit under its own trailer — rather than cross the gate into Codex-held ground. The hearths-gate refused the founding-hearth commit correctly; `--no-verify` was not taken. Law: a handback left in the tree is a crossing that waited its turn — the founding hearth writes the design, the holding hearth lands it, and this row is what tells the Codex hand the dirty B10 is a gift, not a collision.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:220:# ''The carrier's shore'' — the meme hearth landed the 2026-09-13 announce ruling (`crossroadsAnnounceOf` carries `docUrl` at the PUBLIC tier alone; `publicRealmBooksFromDoc` and `announcedRealmBooks` fold a board back to the books a carrier may serve) and wired ONE lane into the founding hearth's `open-node-vessel.ts` — an addition inside the Herm branch's `publicCas` shore, region ⑦ of `docs/pono/vessel-regions`; no line moved. Files crossed: NONE, in the end — the gate refused and `--no-verify` sat outside this hand's reach, so the wiring is HELD IN THE TREE as a handback (one `announcedRealmBooks` call inside the Herm branch's `publicCas` shore, region ⑦ of `docs/pono/vessel-regions`; no line moved), the shape the blob-carriage row names. The lane it feeds, its fold, and its tests all landed on meme ground and stand green without it. The measurement it bought belongs to the holding hearth as much as to this one: a crossroads board keys on the VESSEL's OWN verifying key, so the keeping hearth and the carrier stand in one realm, name one realm doc, and read TWO disjoint public boards. Law: a crossing that MEASURES the holding hearth's ground carries the measurement in its row, not only in the file it touched.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:222:# ''The four stale rooms, measured and NOT edited'' — a founding-hearth spirit re-trued six carriers on free ground (the retired allow-all identity default in `lar-vessel.mem` · `identity-slot.mem` · `lararium-canonical-model.mem`; the lamplighters concession that posed one road as a three-way fork; `handoff.mem`'s COLLISION HANDBACK paragraph, still routing a reader to two settled rulings; `api/pono/rust-toolchain`'s CI claims) and measured FOUR MORE standing on the meme hearth's `docs/pono/**`: `testing-architecture-scout:105·107·109` (witness-all and `gate:fold-ts` both DO run in CI — the fleet globs 34 files and runs 29; the one runner nothing invokes is `lararium-sensorium/scripts`, 989 of the 1016 collected python tests) · `recovery-custody-scout:176` (a recovery-authority compromise reads TERMINAL and "presently open"; delegation stands RULED-REJECTED at `identity-classes:520-529` and the contest window that answers it stands BUILT — `provisional`/`vetoOfCid`/`mintVeto`/`foldPersonaContests`) · `syncer-seams-roundtable:375` ("one inbound edge" measures TWO carriers across three `loulou` sites, and the second wants a replacement exemplar rather than a re-point) · `scale-stories-basket-one:18` (no `lifecycle/*` tag, so ungoverned under `otakiage`'s own law, plus the two retired keys; six inbound carriers and a live assertion in `ahi-ka.test.ts:141` that reds on deletion). Files crossed: NONE — every item sat in the handback carrier `docs/handback-stale-rooms` on unheld ground, each with its file:line, the command that re-derives the number, and suggested replacement prose. Law: a measurement of another hearth's ground crosses by CARRIER, and the carrier ships the RE-DERIVATION beside every number — a scout's citation reads as a claim, and a hearth re-truing its own room off someone else's reading plants a fresh lie with a fresh timestamp. Second law, from the shape: `03ef9b61b` swept for exactly this fault and missed a room ''inside a file it had open'', because a sweep keyed on a phrase finds the phrase. ''Written 2026-09-13'', after the meme hearth closed and the deadlock below dissolved; the standing hearth then re-verified every number itself and enacted all four items. The carrier that held them stood `folded` and went to the fire the same watch (check-in `7d3b3bf5c`, poured `428550a92`, ash `929dc3005`) — ''this row names it as record, and a reader who opens for it finds nothing on disk by design''. Its shape at the moment it stood folded rides in `otakiage#/examples` as DESCRIPTION, under that rite's own law: a stage whose exit runs to deletion cannot be evidenced by a pointer.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:223:# ''The weld that could not expire'' — the founding hearth widened `offering-antigen.test.ts`'s caller scan from one `src/` to the whole workspace (`185dae028`), because `offering.mem` #/must-not puts the first honest caller on the taker's door in `@lares/cli`. No production behaviour moved; the fold stands as uncalled as before. Law: a self-clearing weld whose scan cannot reach the place its caller must appear certifies an absence it never looked for.
